cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below. A peer-reviewed publication is in preparation; please check back for updated citation details."
title: "DeCodeDNA"
abstract: "DeCodeDNA is an end-to-end eDNA metabarcoding analysis pipeline that can be run on everyday laptops. It takes Oxford Nanopore long-read sequencing data from raw POD5 basecalling through quality control, consensus calling, LULU denoising, and taxonomic assignment with BLAST and Kraken2 against MIDORI and MitoFish databases. Developed for the Friday Harbor Labs eDNA summer course by The eDNA Collaborative."
type: software
